@startuml
!theme plain
autonumber

actor User
participant "Frontend" as FE
participant "Backend\n(LangGraph Orchestrator)" as BE
database "Vector Store" as DB
participant "Retriever Node" as Retriever
participant "Grader Node" as Grader
participant "Router" as Router
participant "Generation Node" as Gen
participant "Fallback Node" as Fallback

User -> FE : Submit Query
FE -> BE : Forward Query

note right of BE
  **State Initialization:**
  Initialize state object (query, retrieved_docs,
  filtered_docs, answer, confidence/status)
end note

BE -> Retriever : Trigger graph execution
Retriever -> DB : Fetch relevant chunks
DB --> Retriever : Return chunks

note right of Retriever
  **Retrieval:**
  Fetches relevant chunks from the
  vector store/knowledge layer
end note

Retriever -> Grader : Pass retrieved documents

note right of Grader
  **Grading/Filtering:**
  Evaluate chunk relevance 
  and remove noisy context
end note

Grader -> Router : Pass filtered context

note right of Router
  **Conditional Routing:**
  Check if sufficient high-quality 
  context exists
end note

alt Context is sufficient
    Router -> Gen : Route to Generation
    note right of Gen
      Compose grounded answer 
      using the filtered context
    end note
    Gen --> BE : Return generated answer
    
else Context is insufficient
    Router -> Fallback : Route to Fallback
    note right of Fallback
      Clarification, safe response, 
      or alternate retrieval strategy
    end note
    Fallback --> BE : Return fallback response
end

BE --> FE : Return final response
note right of FE
  **Final Output:**
  Returned with improved grounding 
  and predictable behavior
end note
FE --> User : Display response

@enduml